(Before this fix a double `Free` was completely silent - `Free` on a buffer
 did nothing at all, so there was no first release to repeat. Now the first
 `Free` really releases the block, and a second `Free` on the same variable
 - the slot already holds the shared empty header's own address - is a
 no-op that only sets the error flag; it never munmaps a second time.)

a buffer called data is "hello".
Free data.
Free data.
On error Print "flagged once".
Print "still running".
